# What a whole-tree `prettier --write .` must not touch. The supported invocations are scoped to
# src/ + e2e/ (`npm run format` / `npm run format:check`, and CI's check) — frontend/'s own root
# files (angular.json, README.md, the Playwright configs, .claude/CLAUDE.md) are tool- or
# prose-owned and never agreed to Prettier's config (PR #618's call). This file covers the ad-hoc
# `npx prettier --write .` that someone will eventually type anyway: build output takes minutes to
# rewrite, and package-lock.json's shape is npm's.
dist/
coverage/
.angular/
test-results/
playwright-report/

# npm owns this file's shape; reformatting it only makes the next `npm ci` rewrite it back.
package-lock.json
